This directory holds E3SM component input files staged by Polaris'
`e3sm/init` `component_inputs` workflow.

DO NOT UPLOAD THIS TREE TO THE INPUTDATA SERVER ON ITS OWN.

It is a SUBSET of what E3SM needs to run a new mesh.  It covers the meshes,
initial conditions and graph partitions for MPAS-Ocean and MPAS-Seaice, and
the shared base mesh and SCRIP files.  It does NOT include, among other
things:

  * diagnostic mapping files and region masks
  * E3SM-to-CMIP mapping files
  * iceberg and ice-shelf melt climatologies
  * sea-surface salinity restoring
  * tidal mixing
  * the coefficients for velocity reconstruction

The remaining steps in adding a mesh to E3SM are outside the scope of
Polaris.  Do not try to add a new mesh to E3SM yourself.  Contact an expert on
the E3SM team, such as Jon Wolfe, instead.

The layout under `inputdata/` mirrors where each file belongs in E3SM's
inputdata tree, so files can be copied across once the full set exists.

Ice-shelf cavities are not supported by this workflow.  These files are for
meshes culled with the `calving_front` Antarctic boundary convention, which
have no cavities, and they carry no land-ice fields.
